& [CanonicalRecord: IR4ImplementationActivation] is the processed planning authority for IR4 bounded runtime graph implementation activation slices
  + [canonical_uuid] is 917b6b74-0ebe-40bf-bd03-728a4e04dc09
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is 65f4d1a7-2c4f-45c7-b517-fd27e1b14a72
  + [slice_surface_uuid] is 4cd6c61b-5e8c-47f3-af16-6a80d7017a5f
  + [authority_scope] is IR4 implementation activation slice order, gates, expected outputs, model routing, file inventory, fixture inventory, generated-output proof, dependency decision boundary, implementation boundaries, and forbidden live-control scope
  + [implementation_scope] is bounded runtime graph implementation activation planning and gated implementation slices
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR4_LangGraph_Proof_Runtime_Activation_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR4_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/implementation/IR4_LangGraph_Proof_Runtime_Implementation_Plan.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/fixtures/IR4_Runtime_Graph_Fixture_Plan.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR4_Implementation_Activation_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR4 implementation activation surface
  = must: execute IR4-IA01 first
  = must: run completion review after each IR4 implementation activation slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: preserve generated checkpoints, traces, reports, manifests, caches, fixture outputs, graph state, LangGraph checkpoints, surface state, adapter state, and chat carriers as non-authoritative projections
  = must: preserve SOP artifacts and accepted completion reviews as the truth-bearing records outside runtime graph state
  - never: treat IR4 implementation activation as permission for surface implementation, operations simulator implementation, operations control, or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR4ImplementationActivationSliceSet] is the final IR4 implementation activation slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR4-IA01 bounded implementation activation boundary and dependency decision
  + [slice] is IR4-IA02 fixture source and expected-ledger seed material
  + [slice] is IR4-IA03 graph state and graph contract model implementation
  + [slice] is IR4-IA04 checkpoint and SOP-first interrupt model implementation
  + [slice] is IR4-IA05 pure graph runner implementation without external LangGraph dependency
  + [slice] is IR4-IA06 fixture runner and generated path policy implementation
  + [slice] is IR4-IA07 contract tests and generated-output proof
  + [slice] is IR4-IA08 dependency-authorized LangGraph adapter decision or deferral review
  + [slice] is IR4-IA09 implementation completion review and runtime graph proof pack

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes IR4 implementation activation

& [CanonicalIR4ImplementationActivationGate] is the activation rule for IR4 implementation
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR4-IA01
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA02 until IR4-IA01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA03 until IR4-IA02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA04 until IR4-IA03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA05 until IR4-IA04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA06 until IR4-IA05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA07 until IR4-IA06 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA08 until IR4-IA07 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR4-IA09 until IR4-IA08 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is IR4 implementation proof pack accepted after IR4-IA09

& [CanonicalIR4ImplementationActivationModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR4-IA01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR4-IA02] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA01 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA03] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA02 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA04] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA03 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA05] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA04 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA06] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA05 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA07] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR4-IA06 acceptance
  + [IR4-IA08] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR4-IA09] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: route any authority semantics, graph semantics, checkpoint authority boundary, interrupt/resume contract, dependency-boundary, generated output policy, public API boundary, or safety-boundary change to deeper reasoning
  = must: treat IR4-IA02 through IR4-IA07 as Spark-suitable only while they remain within accepted boundaries and have passing verification oracles

& [CanonicalIR4ImplementationActivationDependencyPolicy] is the dependency decision policy for IR4
  + [initial_dependency_state] is Python standard library only
  + [langgraph_package_state] is gated_until_IR4-IA08
  + [pure_runner_status] is proof-runtime implementation, not final package integration
  + [adapter_status] is decision_or_deferral_only_until_dependency_authorizing_slice_accepts

  = must: keep package installation, lockfile mutation, dependency metadata mutation, and external package imports out of IR4-IA01 through IR4-IA07
  = must: let IR4-IA08 either authorize a later LangGraph adapter slice with explicit dependency instructions or defer dependency work with proof of why the pure runner is sufficient for current runtime proof

